  "raw_text": "Step 1: Let the roots of the polynomial be \\( r, s, t \\). By Vieta's formulas, we know that the sum of the roots taken one at a time is given by:\n\\[ r + s + t = -\\frac{4a}{8} = -\\frac{a}{2}. \\]\n\nStep 2: The sum of the base-2 logarithms of the roots is given as 5. This can be written as:\n\\[ \\log_2(r) + \\log_2(s) + \\log_2(t) = 5. \\]\nUsing the properties of logarithms, this can be rewritten as:\n\\[ \\log_2(rst) = 5. \\]\nThis implies:\n\\[ rst = 2^5 = 32. \\]\n\nStep 3: By Vieta's formulas, the product of the roots taken one at a time is also given by:\n\\[ rst = -\\frac{a}{8}. \\]\nSince we already know \\( rst = 32 \\), we can set up the equation:\n\\[ -\\frac{a}{8} = 32. \\]\nSolving for \\( a \\):\n\\[ a = -256. \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-256}<|im_end|>",
